    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2X5eWJrnGAc1N2tw34GW6Rr)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Reverts #520 (already merged); independent of the other open PRs.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Removes the `devonthink-pdf-grey` package (`dt-pdf-grey`) and its line in `stow-migration/packages.tsv`.\n- Adds `adr/0034-dt-pdf-grey-attempt-rejected.org` (status: rejected) and its row in `adr/README.org`, so the attempt is kept as development history.\n- `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## The attempt and why it failed\n\n- **Goal:** a greyer PDF page in DEVONthink's dark mode; DEVONthink has no setting for it.\n- **Tried (#520):** `dt-pdf-grey` wrote the `PDFBackground` key of `com.devon-technologies.think` (it already held a mid grey, 0.4246723651885986) with `defaults write`, with DEVONthink closed. It saved the originals and had `--reset`, `--quit`, `--relaunch`, `--dry-run`, and an optional `--disable-pdf-dark-mode`.\n- **Findings on Sia's Mac:**\n  - Setting `PDFBackground` (0.2 and other levels) changed nothing visible.\n  - Only `DisablePDFDarkMode = 1` had an effect: the PDF switches to the light appearance, not to a grey.\n  - The stored value had the same types DEVONthink uses (`real` alpha, `string` components), so the write was well formed.\n  - `strings` on the DEVONthink binary shows only `PDFBackground`, `PDFBackgroundColor`, `setPDFBackgroundColor:` and `DisablePDFDarkMode` for PDF colour: no dark-specific or tint key.\n  - `sdef` of DEVONthink has no PDF background property (the `background` matches are text formatting and the imprint command).\n- **Why it failed:**\n  - DEVONthink probably inverts the page itself in dark mode, and nothing exposes the tint.\n  - `PDFBackground` is unused or colours only something small like the page margin (not confirmed).\n  - No preference or AppleScript route sets the colour.\n- **Not built:** a Hammerspoon `hs.canvas` overlay (tints the whole window, shifts highlight colours); Sia declined it.\n- **What still works:** `defaults write com.devon-technologies.think DisablePDFDarkMode -bool true` with DEVONthink closed, for the light appearance.\n- The ADR records all of this as bullets.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Before merging: `dt-pdf-grey --reset --quit --relaunch`, so `PDFBackground` and `DisablePDFDarkMode` are back to the saved original (untested by Claude)\n- [x] After merging and pulling: `ls ~/.local/bin/dt-pdf-grey` is gone; if a dead link stays, `stow -D devonthink-pdf-grey` or remove the link (untested by Claude)\n- [x] `rm -r ~/.local/state/dt-pdf-grey` if it is still there\n- [ ] `adr/README.org` shows the 0034 row and the link opens the ADR\n- [ ] Regression: `dt-open-install` and the Hammerspoon highlight keys still work (untested by Claude)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiB7PrmHwprV4jysmZn\n",
